tart now okay if you  want to go for a phd  next  uh  so reading is just like the baseline  thing beyond reading you have to have  the comprehension you have to have that  and that patience the  the mental argument to actually  comprehend things in a in a in a very  critical fashion not only that you have  to actually also critically analyze what  you're writing or what you are reading  so uh  unlike the kind of textbook reading  whatever little you may have done  earlier  you cannot just accept things as they  are written on the page you have to  critically analyze them try to find out  the flaws in what the author may be  writing so when you're reading a  scientific paper a journal paper you  have to try to find out the gap that is  the hurt and soul of research okay so  you have to have that mental capacity to  try to find a flaws this this habit of  of questioning what the author is  writing may be questioning the very  premise on which the author is basing  his arguments  okay so if again if you have not  developed this habit try to develop this  on this note i would like to point out  that there's something called the  the gre uh so this is an examination  which students have to appear in if they  want to study abroad  especially the us  so uh as part of the gre at least in i  knew that during our time there was an  an important part of the gre which uh  had to do with the composition the some  kind of an essay writing and then you  also had to analyze a piece like you had  to critically appraise a piece  so that is a very very good way of  judging  this kind of a critical analytical  ability of the uh of a prospective phd  candidate uh unfortunately you know in  our indian system as far as i know we do  not have the system we only judge the  students purely on the technical uh  aspects we do not judge them on this  kind of a general critical analytical  ability i wish we could uh we could take  a step in that direction also  now  uh the next thing is communication so  reading is fine  comprehension is fine let's say and then  let's say that your analytical skills  are also up to mark  but suppose  uh you cannot organize your thoughts in  a uh in a nice fashion synthesize what  you have read and understood and  analyzed and then  communicate your ideas then it will be  difficult for you to succeed in a phd  okay so now and this should not be  like a discouragement to you okay  none of us naturally have this ability  okay i mean very rarely a person may be  naturally gifted as a communicator but  that's quite rare okay uh usually we  don't have disabilities so this has to  be developed over time and most phd  students during their phd develop this  thing but what i'm trying to say is that  you should have an open mind towards  this okay you should not think that okay  i will just do the technical thing i  will not go into this this this soft  skills development thing if you if you  have that attitude then you will not be  able to succeed in a phd okay and  communication is such an important thing  it starts with how you communicate with  what you are doing about what you are  doing and what you want to do and what  could be the possible difficulties as  you communicate with your supervisor  your phd advisor okay it starts there  and it goes beyond that as you as you  probably  have to communicate your ideas to your  doctoral scrutiny committee and beyond  that in conferences in various kinds of  presentations and if you go into the  academic client day in and day out you  have to have this communication okay you  have to spend your words  all right  the next thing is that writing  okay now  uh  writing is something which  like holds the key to how smoothly your  phd will go how fast you will complete  your phd and overall how productive you  will be in your phd  okay so no matter how great a research  you have done if you are not able to  write up your results if you are not  able to write up and communicate your  results in the form of papers  then uh it's going to be very very  difficult okay now  of course uh i mean  [Music]  the kind of writing that you have to do  again it will be long-form passages so  uh so this this this ability to write  properly has to be developed to the  fullest extent unless of course you are  going to do a phd in something like pure  mathematics okay then maybe you do not  have to write as much but even in  applied mathematics certainly in  engineering and the sciences you have to  write a lot you have to really explain  what you have what you're doing so the  point that i'm trying to uh  that that i uh want you to ask yourself  is  do you have this habit of writing now i  know usually the answer will be no okay  most of us don't have this habit of  writing especially during an  undergraduate days maybe on rare  occasions some people are interested in  story writing poetry uh  some kind of article writing but that's  those are very rare cases okay usually  we don't have this habit so what i want  you to ask is that okay fine  but at least did you enjoy  the things like pressy writing summary  writing essay writing back when you were  at school so it goes back to that okay  so those were the kinds of exercises  believe it or not which comes  to extreme use during your phd and i'm  not making this up you ask any any  professor uh who has guided students  he will tell you this okay he or she  will tell you this that this is  something which you cannot cannot avoid  you have to write things in long form  you have to express yourself  now  again there is a language barrier okay i  understand this fully  many indian students find it extremely  difficult to write okay but  uh please do not  get into the misconception that this  kind of a problem with writing exists  only with students who have  probably the disadvantage of not having  any training in english because i have  seen  many students who have passed out from  english medium schools who  can understand things very well who are  rational or sound of logic  but when it comes to writing they have a  serious problem okay so it is  you know what it is it is like  like knowing the mechanics of riding a  bike or driving a car and actually being  able to ride a bike and driving a car  okay these are like completely separate  things you you have to know actually how  to ride a bike okay irrespective of the  immense amount of knowledge of mechanics  you have unless you you are you know  that  so you'll fall down okay similarly in  writing you have to uh actually  be  uh you have to go through the process of  knowing how to write okay and that can  only be developed through practice you  have to you have to go through the in  that pain of connecting your thoughts to  the words on the paper  okay so uh  many many students find it difficult  okay despite uh despite maybe even going  to very poor schools they find it  difficult sometimes what happens is that  people who have had a very good school  education they are capable of writing uh  beautifully structured sentences  but  sometimes on the scale of different of  connecting different paragraphs they ah  they completely screw it up okay so  there's a lack of coherency in their  writing some kind of inconsistency  okay  so if you have this ability  great if you don't start  start developing this ability okay or at  least be open to the idea that you have  to have to invest a lot of effort and  time in developing this availability  that that have that open mind and people  who have not had the privilege of going  to an english medium school please don't  feel down okay grammatical mistakes some  kind of shortcomings in vocabulary and  all these things these are like very  cosmetic things this can be  repaired over time there is no problem  the more important thing is that the  maturity of your thought the coherency  and the consistency of your thoughts and  how you can put them in in writing if  you i  i assure you this that if you can if you  have developed this muscle of connecting  your thoughts this organized thoughts  coherent thoughts in writing even in  your own mother term or that of the  language in which you have had your  schooling  i i assure you you can do the same thing  in english also there will be some  barrier but that can be overcome but  that is not as tough as a barrier as  not being able to uh to make this  transition from your thoughts to your uh  words uh to the written word  okay so i've spoken quite a lot on  various issues now these are the things  which i think are uh are are extremely  important  now please note that i have i have uh  i've not mentioned anything regarding  the uh some of the personality traits  okay so this video is already gone quite  a long i i won't uh drag it uh anymore  so  uh you tell me in your in the comments  uh if you would like to have another  video on those aspects like uh the  ability to take criticism uh the  uh the patients aspect the uh the  the various kinds of other personality  traits which may be required for uh  success in a phd and uh i'll try to  think seriously about making a separate  video for that  but before i end i want to just point  out one thing that i have posed a number  of questions to this video  maybe there are  19 points and  if you see that maybe you are saying yes  to uh six of them and maybe three or  four are saying no doesn't mean that it  makes you unsuitable okay  as long as you have an open mind as i've  said earlier multiple times it's fine  okay of course if out of nine or ten  questions you are saying no to  everything then maybe seriously rethink  about joining a phd okay but i'm sure  it'll not it'll not be like that just by  the very fact that you are watching this  video and  since i have spoken such a lot about  analyzing uh critically thinking about  the written word or hearing what you are  saying uh i i invite you to critically  appreciate this particular video itself  okay so as a 